<title>BELGIUM: Swiss Re, SAFR withdraw EU takeover notice.</title>
<headline>Swiss Re, SAFR withdraw EU takeover notice.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Monday that French reinsurance firm Societe Anonyme Francaise de Reassurances (SAFR) and Swiss Reinsurance Co (Swiss Re) had withdrawn a request for Commission approval of a takeover deal.</p>
<p>The companies had submitted the deal, under which Swiss Re would have acquired the shares of SAFR held by Assurances Generales de France and French insurance group Athena, to the Commission on March 7.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement that the notification had been withdrawn on April 8. It gave no details, but Swiss Re said on March 31 it would sell SAFR to Bermuda-based PartnerRe Ltd after it had completed its acquisition of the Paris-based reinsurer.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
